{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:44:27.235Z","data":{"text":"Both the task verify and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass on the final tree.\n\nSummary of what I did:\n- `src/docs/markdown.ts` — pure renderers for the index, capability pages and ADR pages, returning a `Map` of relative path to content (one trailing newline each, no timestamps).\n- `src/docs/docs-command.ts` — `docsCommand(options)` builds the site, writes under `out`, removes stale `.md` files directly in `capabilities/` and `adrs/`, prints `wrote <n> pages to <out>`, and returns the written paths.\n- `src/docs/slice.ts` — the `docs` slice with the `docs` config block and the `docs` command in `Inspection`, loading `docs-command.js` via `import()`.\n- `src/cli/slices.ts` — registered the slice.\n- `README.md` — added `osq docs [--out <dir>]` after `osq spec`.\n- `tests/docs-command.test.ts` — proves both scenarios plus the registration/config checks.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/175-capability-pages/.run/results/3.md`."}}
